// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_cram_four_words.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: stream_cram's per-op burst ceiling, at the FIRST width it refuses.
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: "4 colours exceeds RASTER_BURST_MAX_CRAM (3)"
//
// WHY FOUR AND NOT FIVE. Five is refused by the arithmetic alone — 4 x 26 = 104 against a
// 122.9-cycle window leaves 18.9 for margins that want 30 — so a poison there would be
// testing a sum, and the sum is already asserted at module level beside the margins. Four is
// the interesting width: it FITS that sum with 14.9 cycles to spare, and is refused anyway,
// because the solver quantizes to whole `dbf` iterations and the nearest one leaves the first
// write 0.9 cycles inside the early margin (raster.emp, the burst-ceiling note). This case is
// the one that would go quiet if someone read the arithmetic, concluded four was fine, and
// raised the ceiling without re-reading the landing.
//
// THE FRAGMENT QUOTES THE CEILING'S VALUE so that a future raise cannot pass by editing one
// constant: it has to come here, change the number, and in doing so notice that the number
// has a measured argument behind it.
//
// EXACTLY ONE DIAGNOSTIC, and the hook is chosen to keep it that way. `raster_words` walks
// `op_size` and nothing else, so the only guard this module reaches is the constructor's.
// Two others WOULD fire on this op list if it went further and both have their own cases:
// `fire()`'s per-fire ceiling (dodged here by building the RasterFire variant directly, the
// same dodge poison_landing_late documents) and `check_landings` (dodged by not calling
// `raster_program` — and note it would NOT fire at four words, since 0.9 cycles of early
// slack is still positive; that is precisely why the constructor ceiling has to exist rather
// than being left to the landing guard).
//
// NO IMPORTS, like every ordinary author's module: raster_dsl and engine.vdp are
// COMPTIME_HELPERS members, glob-injected into every module by the real build. See
// the README on why the lane cannot reproduce that injection yet.
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_cram_four_words

const POISON_CRAM_FOUR = [
    RasterFire.Fire(100, [stream_cram($42, [$0E0E, $0E0E, $0E0E, $0E0E])]),
]

// THE ELABORATION HOOK — see poison_four_bands.emp's note. Trivially-true predicate;
// the diagnostic under test comes from inside the call.
ensure(raster_words(POISON_CRAM_FOUR) > 0,
       "poison_cram_four_words: raster_words returned nothing — this poison no longer reaches the guard it targets")
